  "narrative": {
    "intro": "CACI Federal has obligated $2.8B in federal contract obligations in FY2026 to date. CACI Federal won 216 awards in the period, with an average award size of $12.9M, and obligations fell 20.9% year over year. Obligations by fiscal year show $1.3B in FY21, $1.7B in FY22, $2.3B in FY23, $2.8B in FY24, $3.5B in FY25, and $2.8B in FY26. The Department of Defense is the largest buyer, with $1.5B in obligations, followed by the General Services Administration at $950M and the Department of Homeland Security at $215M. Computer Systems Design Services is the largest market by NAICS at $1.1B, followed by Engineering Services at $648M and Investigation and Personal Background Check Services at $258M. CACI Federal also shows activity in NASA at $135M and in Research and Development in the Physical, Engineering, and Life Sciences at $231M. The numbers reported are contract obligations except where noted as total contract values in award tables.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "Who are CACI Federal's biggest buyers?",
        "body": "The Department of Defense obligated $1.5B with CACI Federal in FY2026 to date. The General Services Administration obligated $950M and the Department of Homeland Security obligated $215M. National Aeronautics and Space Administration obligated $135M, and the Department of the Interior obligated $26.4M."
      },
      {
        "heading": "What does CACI Federal sell to the government?",
        "body": "Computer Systems Design Services is the largest market for CACI Federal at $1.1B in obligations. Engineering Services account for $648M and Investigation and Personal Background Check Services account for $258M. Additional significant markets include Research and Development in the Physical, Engineering, and Life Sciences at $231M and All Other Professional, Scientific, and Technical Services at $192M."
      }
    ]
